## 1. Current Security Assessment

### Overall Security Posture: 🔴 CRITICAL — NOT PRODUCTION-READY

The platform exhibits **systemic, fundamental security failures** across every layer. This is not a matter of hardening — the security model is architecturally absent. The system operates on an implicit trust model: anyone who can reach the Supabase anon key (which is embedded in the frontend JavaScript bundle and visible to every browser on Earth) can read, write, and delete any data in the entire system.

### Critical Vulnerability Summary

| Severity | Count | Category |
|----------|-------|----------|
| 🔴 CRITICAL | 14 | Authentication bypass, credential exposure, privilege escalation, data exfiltration |
| 🟠 HIGH | 18 | Missing authorization, unprotected APIs, insecure file storage, AI data leakage |
| 🟡 MEDIUM | 11 | Weak password policy, missing CSRF, no rate limiting on app-level, missing audit trail |
| 🔵 LOW | 4 | Missing security headers, no CSP, verbose error messages |

