## 3. Authorization Assessment

### Current State: 🔴 CRITICAL — AUTHORIZATION IS ABSENT

> [!CAUTION]
> **There is zero authorization enforcement anywhere in this application.** Every authenticated user can access every page, query every table, and modify any record. The navigation menu cosmetically hides links, but does not prevent access.

### Page-Level Authorization Audit

| Route Segment | Expected Access | Actual Enforcement | Vulnerability |
|--------------|----------------|-------------------|---------------|
| `/admin/*` | Admin only | ❌ None — any user can navigate here | Employee can view/edit all admin pages |
| `/hr/*` | HR only | ❌ None | Candidate can access HR recruitment, payroll management |
| `/team-lead/*` | Team Lead only | ❌ None | Employee can access team lead approvals, team management |
| `/employee/*` | Matching Employee | ❌ None | Any employee can view any other employee's data |
| `/candidate/*` | Matching Candidate | ❌ None | Any candidate can view other candidates' assessments, messages |
| `/apply/:formId` | Public | ✅ Correct | Publicly accessible as intended |
| `/assessment/:token` | Token-holder | ⚠️ Token-based | Token validation exists but no rate limiting on token guessing |

### API/Query-Level Authorization Audit

| Query Pattern | Expected | Actual |
|--------------|----------|--------|
| `profiles.select('*')` | Scoped to self or team | ❌ Returns ALL profiles to any user |
| `complaints.select('*')` | Scoped to relevant role | ❌ Returns all complaints to any user |
| `work_logs.select('*')` | Own logs or team logs | ❌ All work logs accessible |
| `candidates.select('*')` | HR/Admin only | ❌ Any user can read candidate data |
| `payroll` data | Own payroll or Admin/HR | ❌ Simulated but profiles accessible for salary derivation |
| `tasks.update(...)` | Assignee or creator | ❌ Any user can modify any task |
| `profiles.update({role: ...})` | Admin only | ❌ Any user can update any profile's role |
| `leaves.select('*')` | Own or team manager | ❌ All leave records accessible |

### Shared Component Cross-Role Contamination

Several routes render the **same component** across different roles with no authorization differentiation:

| Component | Used By Routes | Risk |
|-----------|---------------|------|
| `AdminPayroll` | `/admin/payroll`, `/team-lead/payroll`, `/employee/payroll` | The same admin payroll component is reused for all roles — meaning employees see the admin payroll view |
| `AdminMasterDirectory` | `/admin/directory`, `/hr/directory` | HR gets the admin master directory with full admin powers |
| `AdminAnalytics` | `/admin/analytics`, `/hr/analytics` | HR gets unrestricted admin analytics |
| `AdminPresence` | `/admin/presence`, `/hr/presence` | HR gets full admin presence view |
| `AdminComplaints` | `/admin/complaints`, `/hr/complaints` | HR sees admin complaint view including escalated items |
| `AdminApprovals` | `/admin/approvals`, `/hr/approvals` | HR gets admin-level approval powers |

