## 4. RBAC Architecture

### Current State: No RBAC Exists

Roles are stored as a text string (`'admin' | 'team_lead' | 'employee' | 'hr' | 'candidate'`) in two places:
1. `user_metadata.role` (mutable by user)
2. `profiles.role` (overwritten on every login from user_metadata)

There is no roles table, no permissions table, no role hierarchy, and no enforcement layer.

### Target Enterprise RBAC Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Role Hierarchy"
        SUPER_ADMIN["Super Admin<br/>(System Owner)"]
        ADMIN["Admin<br/>(Org Administrator)"]
        HR_MANAGER["HR Manager<br/>(HR Department Head)"]
        HR["HR Specialist<br/>(HR Staff)"]
        RECRUITER["Recruiter<br/>(Hiring Focus)"]
        DEPT_MANAGER["Department Manager<br/>(Multi-Team)"]
        TEAM_LEAD["Team Lead<br/>(Single Team)"]
        EMPLOYEE["Employee<br/>(Staff)"]
        CANDIDATE["Candidate<br/>(External Applicant)"]
    end
    
    SUPER_ADMIN --> ADMIN
    ADMIN --> HR_MANAGER
    HR_MANAGER --> HR
    HR_MANAGER --> RECRUITER
    ADMIN --> DEPT_MANAGER
    DEPT_MANAGER --> TEAM_LEAD
    TEAM_LEAD --> EMPLOYEE
    HR --> CANDIDATE
```

### Target Database Schema

```sql
-- Roles table (immutable reference data)
CREATE TABLE roles (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    name TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL, -- 'super_admin', 'admin', 'hr_manager', etc.
    display_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    hierarchy_level INT NOT NULL, -- 0=highest, 100=lowest
    is_internal BOOLEAN DEFAULT true, -- false for 'candidate'
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

-- Permissions table (granular actions)
CREATE TABLE permissions (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    resource TEXT NOT NULL,      -- 'profiles', 'payroll', 'candidates', etc.
    action TEXT NOT NULL,        -- 'read', 'write', 'delete', 'approve', 'export'
    scope TEXT NOT NULL,         -- 'own', 'team', 'department', 'organization'
    UNIQUE(resource, action, scope)
);

-- Role-Permission mapping
CREATE TABLE role_permissions (
    role_id UUID REFERENCES roles(id),
    permission_id UUID REFERENCES permissions(id),
    PRIMARY KEY (role_id, permission_id)
);

-- User-Role assignment (replaces text role on profiles)
CREATE TABLE user_roles (
    user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    role_id UUID REFERENCES roles(id),
    assigned_by UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id),
    assigned_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now(),
    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, role_id)
);
```

### Role Assignment Rules

| Rule | Enforcement |
|------|-------------|
| Only Super Admin can assign Admin role | Database trigger + RLS policy |
| Only Admin/HR Manager can assign HR, Recruiter, Manager roles | Database trigger + RLS policy |
| Only Admin/Team Lead can assign Employee role | Via approval workflow |
| Candidate role assigned on self-registration | Automatic on registration |
| Role changes require approval + audit log | Dual approval for privilege escalation |
| No self-role-modification | Enforced by RLS (`auth.uid() != target_user_id` for role writes) |

