## 6. RLS Strategy

### Current State: 🔴 NO RLS POLICIES EXIST

There is no evidence of any Row Level Security policies in the codebase. All tables are fully readable and writable by any authenticated user holding the anon key.

### Target RLS Policy Design

> [!IMPORTANT]
> RLS must be enabled on **every single table** in the database. There must be zero exceptions.

#### Helper Function (role resolver — server-side)

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.get_user_role()
RETURNS TEXT AS $$
  SELECT role FROM public.user_roles ur
  JOIN public.roles r ON ur.role_id = r.id
  WHERE ur.user_id = auth.uid()
  ORDER BY r.hierarchy_level ASC
  LIMIT 1;
$$ LANGUAGE sql SECURITY DEFINER STABLE;

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.is_admin_or_hr()
RETURNS BOOLEAN AS $$
  SELECT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.user_roles ur
    JOIN public.roles r ON ur.role_id = r.id
    WHERE ur.user_id = auth.uid()
    AND r.name IN ('super_admin', 'admin', 'hr_manager', 'hr')
  );
$$ LANGUAGE sql SECURITY DEFINER STABLE;

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.get_team_member_ids()
RETURNS UUID[] AS $$
  SELECT array_agg(id) FROM public.profiles
  WHERE team_lead_id = auth.uid()
$$ LANGUAGE sql SECURITY DEFINER STABLE;
```

#### Per-Table RLS Policies

| Table | SELECT Policy | INSERT Policy | UPDATE Policy | DELETE Policy |
|-------|--------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|
| `profiles` | Own row always; team rows for TL/Manager; all rows for Admin/HR | Self-registration only (via trigger) | Own non-role fields; Admin/HR can update all | Admin only (soft delete via ARCHIVED status) |
| `work_logs` | Own logs; team logs for TL; all for Admin/HR | Own user_id only | Own active logs only | Admin only |
| `tasks` | Assigned/created by self; team tasks for TL; all for Admin | TL/Manager/Admin | Assignee can update status; creator can update details | Creator/Admin |
