## 11. Audit Logging Architecture

### Current State: 🔴 NO AUDIT LOGGING EXISTS

There is zero audit logging anywhere in the application. No database triggers, no application-level logging, no access tracking, no change history.

### Target Audit Logging Architecture

#### Audit Events to Capture

| Category | Events | Priority |
|----------|--------|----------|
| **Authentication** | Login success, login failure, logout, password change, password reset request, MFA enrollment, MFA verification | 🔴 P0 |
| **Authorization** | Access denied events, privilege escalation attempts, role changes | 🔴 P0 |
| **User Management** | User creation, user deactivation, role assignment, profile updates | 🔴 P0 |
| **Data Access** | Payroll viewed, candidate data accessed, resume downloaded, document accessed, export initiated | 🟠 P1 |
| **Data Modification** | Record created, record updated (with before/after diff), record deleted | 🟠 P1 |
| **HR Actions** | Leave approved/rejected, complaint resolved, offer issued, onboarding completed | 🟠 P1 |
| **ATS Events** | Application submitted, assessment graded, interview scheduled/completed, offer sent, candidate status change | 🟠 P1 |
| **AI Events** | AI query made, data sent to external AI, AI recommendation generated | 🟡 P2 |
| **System Events** | Edge Function invocations, storage operations, realtime channel subscriptions | 🟡 P2 |

#### Audit Log Schema

```sql
CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    event_type TEXT NOT NULL,          -- 'AUTH_LOGIN', 'DATA_READ', 'DATA_WRITE', etc.
    event_category TEXT NOT NULL,      -- 'authentication', 'authorization', 'data_access', etc.
    actor_id UUID,                     -- auth.uid() of the person performing the action
    actor_role TEXT,                   -- Role at time of action
    actor_ip INET,                    -- IP address
    actor_user_agent TEXT,            -- Browser/device fingerprint
    target_table TEXT,                -- Table affected
    target_id UUID,                   -- Row ID affected
    action TEXT NOT NULL,             -- 'SELECT', 'INSERT', 'UPDATE', 'DELETE'
    old_values JSONB,                 -- Previous state (for updates/deletes)
    new_values JSONB,                 -- New state (for inserts/updates)
    metadata JSONB,                   -- Additional context
    severity TEXT DEFAULT 'INFO',     -- 'INFO', 'WARNING', 'CRITICAL'
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

-- Immutable: only system can insert, nobody can update/delete
ALTER TABLE audit_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "No one can modify audit logs" ON audit_logs FOR ALL USING (false);
CREATE POLICY "System can insert audit logs" ON audit_logs FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (true);
CREATE POLICY "Admin can read audit logs" ON audit_logs FOR SELECT USING (public.is_admin_or_hr());

-- Partition by month for performance
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_created ON audit_logs USING BRIN (created_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_actor ON audit_logs (actor_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_target ON audit_logs (target_table, target_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_type ON audit_logs (event_type);
```

#### Implementation Strategy

1. **Database Triggers** — For all INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE operations on sensitive tables (auto-capture old/new values)
2. **Edge Function Middleware** — Wrap all API calls with audit logging (captures actor, IP, user agent)
3. **Client-Side Event Emitter** — For UI events (page views, exports, searches)
4. **Retention** — 7 years for compliance; 90 days hot storage (PostgreSQL), then archive to cold storage (S3/GCS)
5. **Tamper Protection** — Audit log table is append-only with no UPDATE/DELETE permissions for any role

