| **Assume breach** | 🔴 Not applied | No monitoring, no detection, no containment capability |
| **Verify explicitly** | 🔴 Not applied | No per-request authorization check; role checked once at login |
| **Use just-in-time access** | 🔴 Not applied | Permanent access to all resources once authenticated |
| **Micro-segmentation** | 🔴 Not applied | No network segmentation; all resources on same Supabase instance |
| **End-to-end encryption** | ⚠️ Partial | HTTPS for transit; no encryption at rest; no E2E for sensitive fields |

### Target Zero Trust Architecture

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|---------------|
| **Identity Verification** | Every API call verified via JWT + RLS; session validated on each request; MFA for privileged operations |
| **Device Trust** | Optional: device fingerprinting, certificate-based auth for managed devices |
| **Micro-Segmentation** | Separate Supabase schemas for HR data vs operational data; separate storage buckets with distinct policies |
| **Least Privilege** | RLS policies enforce minimum required access; time-boxed elevated access for admin operations |
| **Continuous Validation** | Re-authenticate for sensitive operations (payroll, role changes, data exports); session health checks every 15 minutes |
| **Assume Breach** | Comprehensive audit logging; anomaly detection; automated response; encrypted data at rest so breach exposure is limited |

